8. GRAVITY IMPLEMENTATION
-------------------------

Gravity is represented using an external body-force multiplier:

gamma = g / g_Earth

Documented gravity conditions:

1.00 g  = Earth
0.75 g  = intermediate reduced gravity
0.50 g  = intermediate reduced gravity
0.38 g  = Mars
0.16 g  = Moon
0.00 g  = microgravity approximation

The six-level gravity sweep is part of the documented computational design.

The 0.75 g and 0.50 g conditions serve as intermediate response points,
whereas 1.00 g, 0.38 g, 0.16 g and 0.00 g represent the principal physical
gravity environments.


9. MESH
--------

Documented mesh strategy:

Tetrahedral coarse / medium / fine mesh series.

Mesh selection must be based on a predefined convergence criterion.

The recovered verification registry documents a target of:

Fine-versus-medium variation ≤2%

However, patient-level convergence values must only be reported as
completed verification results when supported by actual mesh exports or
COMSOL execution evidence.


10. SOLVER
----------

Documented numerical formulation:

Fully coupled nonlinear finite-element solution using a Newton-type
nonlinear solver.

Solver convergence must be documented using retained solver output.

A numerical residual value must not be represented as an executed result
unless the corresponding solver export/log exists.


