15. EVIDENCE HIERARCHY
---------------------

Each computational statement must be assigned one of four evidence classes:

CLASS 1 — SPECIFIED
The parameter or method is documented as part of the intended model.

CLASS 2 — EXECUTED
The model was actually run and an execution artifact exists.

CLASS 3 — VERIFIED
The execution has been checked against a predefined numerical criterion.

CLASS 4 — MANUSCRIPT-REPORTED
The result is sufficiently traceable to an underlying execution artifact to
be included as a quantitative study result.

A Class 1 specification must never be silently converted into a Class 2,
3, or 4 result.


